@startuml client_connection_try_queue_message_activity
title ClientConnection - queued message admission

start
:TryQueueMessage(message, callback);
note right
    Entry: the caller holds send_mutex_.
    Message-size and lifecycle checks belong to the API caller.
end note
if (send_pool_ is empty?) then (yes)
    :Return false without reserving a command;
    stop
else (no)
    :Take the front free command;
endif
:Remove the command from send_pool_;
:Copy message bytes into command.message;
:Move callback into command.callback;
:Append the command to the back of send_queue_;
:Return true with the caller's lock still held;
stop

legend
    send_storage_ retains ownership of the command and its message storage.
    Intrusive membership moves from the free pool to the FIFO send queue.
    Admission does not send, claim the reply slot, or arm queue dispatch.
    The caller turns false into ENOBUFS and decides whether to schedule work.
    Empty versus non-empty callback selects SEND versus REQUEST at dispatch.
endlegend

@enduml